(Beginner to Advanced)
A structured roadmap to become a Cloud & DevOps Engineer by mastering core concepts, tools, and real-world workflows.

##📌 1. Linux Fundamentals

Learn Linux because most servers run on Linux.
Topics:

•File System Structure
•Basic Linux Commands
•File Permissions (chmod, chown)
•Users & Groups
•Process Management (ps, top, kill)
•Practice:
•Create files/folders using terminal
•Manage permissions
•Monitor running processes


##🌐 2. Networking Basics

Strong networking knowledge is essential for DevOps.
Topics:

•IP Addressing
•DNS
•HTTP vs HTTPS
•Ports & Protocols
•Client-Server Architecture
•Practice:
•Use ping, curl, netstat
•Understand how websites work


##🔧 3. Git & GitHub

Version control is mandatory for DevOps workflows.
Topics:

•git init, git add, git commit
•Push / Pull
•Branching
•Merge & Conflict Resolution
•Practice:
•Create repositories
•Collaborate using branches
•Push projects to GitHub


##🐍 4. Scripting (Python / Bash)

Automation is the heart of DevOps.
Topics:

•Variables
•Loops
•Conditions
•Functions
•Simple Automation Scripts
•Practice:
•Backup scripts
•File cleanup automation
•Health check scripts


##☁️ 5. Cloud Computing (AWS Recommended)

Cloud is the modern infrastructure platform.
Core Services:

•EC2 (Virtual Servers)
•S3 (Storage)
•IAM (Users / Roles / Policies)
•VPC (Networking Basics)

Concepts:

•Public vs Private Servers
•Security Groups
•Key Pair Authentication


##🐳 6. Docker

Containerization makes deployment easier.
Topics:

•Docker Images
•Docker Containers
•Dockerfile
•Docker Hub
•Practice:
•Build custom images
•Run containers
•Deploy applications inside containers


##⚙️ 7. CI/CD Pipeline

Automate build, test, and deployment process.
Tools:

•GitHub Actions
•Jenkins
•GitLab CI/CD
•Pipeline Flow:
•Code → Build → Test → Deploy
•Goal:
•Fully automated deployments


##☸️ 8. Kubernetes

Used to manage containers at scale.
Topics:

•Pods
•Deployments
•Services
•Scaling
•Namespaces
•Practice:
•Deploy containerized apps
•Scale applications
•Rolling updates
